# Every path is served by the app, not by the host.
#
# The game routes in the browser, so /profile exists only once index.html has
# loaded and React Router has read the URL. A static host knows nothing about
# that: asked for /profile it looks for a file of that name, finds none, and
# returns its own 404 before the app ever runs. Which means a refresh, or a
# shared link to anything but the home page, breaks.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL must stay as the player typed it, or the router
# has nothing to route on.
/*    /index.html   200
